{"paper": "CHSL-Tier1-08-Jul-2024-Shift4.pdf", "status": "ok", "mode": "sequential", "splitter": "qdot", "section_slice": true, "extracted_count": 25, "tagged_count": 25, "questions": [{"n": 1, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "Management", "added": false}, {"text": "Engineering", "added": false}, {"text": "Arts", "added": false}, {"text": "Science", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 2, "text": "In an election contested by two candidates, one candidate got 42% of the total votes and still lost by 800 votes. Find the total number of votes that were cast.", "options": [{"text": "7000", "added": false}, {"text": "2000", "added": false}, {"text": "8000", "added": false}, {"text": "5000", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "basic-percentage", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 3, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "Kiwi, 23", "added": false}, {"text": "Apple, 28", "added": false}, {"text": "Orange, 23", "added": false}, {"text": "Kiwi, 22", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 4, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 5, "text": "The distance between the centres of two circles is 81 cm, and their radii are 42 cm and 51 cm. What is the length (in cm) of the direct common tangent to the circles?", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Circles-Polygons", "sub": "tangents-and-chords", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 6, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "7 : 10", "added": false}, {"text": "7 : 13", "added": false}, {"text": "7 : 15", "added": false}, {"text": "17 : 10", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 7, "text": "Ram is 20 years older than Rahul. ‘n’ years ago Ram was thrice as old as Rahul. ‘2n’ years from now the ratio of the ages of Ram and Rahul will be 15 : 11. What is the value of ‘n’?", "options": [{"text": "15", "added": false}, {"text": "10", "added": false}, {"text": "30", "added": false}, {"text": "20", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "ratio-basics", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 8, "text": "Which of the following statements is INCORRECT about the circle?", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Geometry", "sub": "lines-and-angles", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 9, "text": "The inner and outer radii of a hemispherical wooden bowl are 6 cm and 8 cm, respectively. Its entire surface has to be polished and the cost of polishing π cm2 is Rs.50. How much will it cost to polish the bowl?", "options": [{"text": "Rs.12,000", "added": false}, {"text": "Rs.10,000", "added": false}, {"text": "Rs.11,600", "added": false}, {"text": "Rs.11,400", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 10, "text": "A man can row a boat at speed 8 km/h in still water. It takes thrice as long to row upstream as it does to row downstream. Find the speed of the stream (in km/h).", "options": [{"text": "5", "added": false}, {"text": "4", "added": false}, {"text": "6", "added": false}, {"text": "3", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Boats-Streams", "sub": "upstream-downstream", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 11, "text": "The value of a machine depreciates every year by 5%. If the present value of the machine is ₹80,000, what will be its value after 2 years?", "options": [{"text": "₹72,200", "added": false}, {"text": "₹74,400", "added": false}, {"text": "₹74,000", "added": false}, {"text": "₹72,000", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "increase-decrease", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 12, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 13, "text": "If A : B = 2 : 3 and B : C = 7 : 8, find A : C.", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 14, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 15, "text": "Two triangles ABC and DEF are similar. The smallest side of ABC is equal to 15 units. If the sides of ABC are in the ratio 3 ∶ 4 ∶ 5, and the area of DEF is half of the area of ABC, then what is the largest side of DEF (in units)?", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 2D", "sub": "triangle-and-quadrilaterals", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 16, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 17, "text": "Two cubes, each of edge 5 cm, are joined face to face. Find the surface area of the cuboid thus formed.", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "cube-cuboid", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 18, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "9.12%", "added": false}, {"text": "8.33%", "added": false}, {"text": "8.20%", "added": false}, {"text": "7.25%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 19, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 20, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 21, "text": "", "opti